  "finding": "Leaf Monkey retains the eyes, nose, lips, rounded muzzle, ears and full visible chin contour above the scarf in source and battle clips and lit opposite/underside views. The leaf cap and neck remain seated with the head during turns and falls. Shoulders, forearms, hands, hips, bent knees, toes and long curled tail stay attached to and follow the body through step, hop, lean, strike, fall, revive and recovery. All nine actual battle technique sequences preserve the leg roots with the torso and return coherently to idle. The24 advancing idle frames and16 atlas cells show no visible collapse, torn face, detached limb or distortion.",
